A||N||8||Elenor84||Swapping Roof's!||||6||
Z||000000||Elenor84||01-26-2001||01:26 AM||||Hey guys...I'm planning on going out and buying a new roof for my car that has a sunroof in it...now I read on another post that I can just simply swap roofs...is this true???<BR>tia<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||6
Z||000001||RaeQwan||01-26-2001||01:57 AM||||Thats true.. the spaceframe is already setup for the sunroof.. all Fiero's are cept the ttop cars.. you will need a new headliner though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Ray - AIM: WookieeNC<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Fiero Coupe</A> - <A HREF="http://www.CarolinaFieros.com" TARGET=_blank>Carolina Fieros</A> - <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/dearabu/" TARGET=_blank>Dear Abu</A> - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.net" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Network</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||01-26-2001||02:07 AM||||Now I'm kinda confused...I may just be dumb but could u define "headliner" for me?  thx<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||01-26-2001||02:27 AM||||The headliner is the cloth on the inside of the car above your head. You will need the roof, glass, hinges, handle assembly, the inside headliner, the seal, and the plastic trim that holds the headliner to the roof around the sunroof opening. Basically just grab everything off the donor car. You need to remove the headliner to access the bolts from inside the car. To remove the headliner, all the plastic trim panels by the top of the door frame, the inside sail panel covers, the map light, the 3rd brake light (if it is there) and sunvisors need to be removed. Caution, the headliner can crack easily if you try to yank it out.<BR>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||01-26-2001||02:43 AM||||Oreif is right on all of that - also, take care when removing the roof panel, here in the shop when we make a sunroof conversion I take out the fender bolts and lay the fenders back (the only way you will get the roof panel off since the panel also surrounds the windshield) and take extreme care when lifting the side pillars of the roof panel - the adhesive is very strong and prying on it could crack your windshield (or, even worse, crack the roof panel pillars after you have done most of the work to remove it!) -- the easiest way is to use a piano wire or a cable saw (I use a cable saw designed to cut plastic pipe) - work the cable saw back and forth and up (or down) at the same time to separate the pillers from the car body.......simply put, don't <I>force</I> the roof panel up or it will crack!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Elenor84||01-26-2001||02:53 AM||||From what my sourse has told me the sunroof glass is missing but I'm sure I can find that somewere here in canada...but everything else is there...so take everythign a?  What do u think I should offer this scrap yard for the whole shot?  Thx...<BR>and I'm also hoping there is a fast back pannel there to..how much do u think thats worth?<BR>thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000006||Greg Piet||01-26-2001||11:08 AM||||I have 3 vista vent(sunroof) pieces, and I am sure others have more than I do.  My spares have been acquired at wreckingyards, and they are plentiful where I am in the US.  But if all else fails I am sure someone here will be able to sell you one as well.<P>As far as what to offer the yard, its kind of hard for me to tell you.  Depending on its overall quality, and if the paint matches already (or really frickin close).   I know that I want another rear clip and if I get a red one that matches close to mine from a junkyard I would pay 250 US if it was in really good shape and I would have the sail panels attached when I bought it, the gas door, the trim, the marker lights... but that is just me.  And that is not for the roof piece as well (You were asking about the entire rear/roof section right)<P>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 01-26-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 01-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||TOM||01-27-2001||01:50 AM||||Also get the parts to stow the glass panel under the hood when removed. There is a long plastic piece and two small metal tabs. And if its there get the wind deflector also.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||01-27-2001||12:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TOM:<BR><B>Also get the parts to stow the glass panel under the hood when removed. There is a long plastic piece and two small metal tabs. And if its there get the wind deflector also.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Its amazing how much air that little 2'' piece of plastic blocks!! With the deflector in you dont get your hair blown even with the glass out.<BR>||||reg||1
